{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/claude-code-settings.json",
  "_comment": [
    "PANG workspace — shared Claude Code permissions.",
    "",
    "This file is committed. It pre-approves the dev-loop commands that every",
    "contributor (and every fresh Claude Code session) needs in order to",
    "execute the doctrine in CLAUDE.md without re-prompting on each command.",
    "",
    "Rules for what lives here:",
    "  1. Only additive, non-destructive patterns. Reads, builds, lints,",
    "     typechecks, mock evals, local dev servers, harness runs. No",
    "     `rm -rf /`, no `git push --force`, no blanket `Bash(*)`.",
    "  2. Patterns must be specific. `Bash(npm run test:e2e:*)` not `Bash(*)`.",
    "  3. Destructive or per-machine commands stay in `settings.local.json`",
    "     (gitignored). Examples: `kill <pid>`, one-off `cp` of assets,",
    "     cloudflared tunnel download, `rm -rf .next`.",
    "  4. A new pattern earns its way in only if it's part of the standard",
    "     dev loop for this repo. If it was useful once, it belongs local.",
    "",
    "If you're unsure whether something belongs here: it doesn't. Add it to",
    "`.claude/settings.local.json` (or answer the prompt once) and promote",
    "later if it keeps showing up."
  ],
